From 801cb82ad8320011140a81d38a41d9f53412da48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <122653016+Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:21:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] XHTTP: Hold upload windows to the queue a PING sees

Larger upload windows let a greedy upload fill the queue at the client's
bottleneck, which the server's kernel cannot see. A PING's ACK waits in
that queue, so the server now compares each PING round trip with the
round trip of the empty path: past half of it the upload window stops
growing, past all of it the window shrinks by a quarter, once per PING
sample and never below what the reader takes per empty round trip. A
client governing its download does the same.

The empty path's round trip is the lowest PING of the connection, the
first of which goes out as soon as the connection is up. The kernel's
min_rtt is preferred when it is within a factor of four, since the
first ACK can wait behind data sent in slow start; further below, a TCP
proxy sits in front and the PING is kept.
